Article 2 (Duties) The Strategic Command (hereinafter referred to as the "Command") shall perform the following duties:
1. Formulation, preparation, execution, and control of operational plans for deterring and responding to enemy nuclear attacks and strategic-level attacks involving weapons of mass destruction (hereinafter referred to as "nuclear and weapons-of-mass-destruction attacks");
2. Military cooperation with the United States in connection with the implementation of extended deterrence;
3. Integrated employment of strategic capabilities (including space, cyber, and electromagnetic-spectrum capabilities; hereinafter the same shall apply) for deterring and responding to nuclear and weapons-of-mass-destruction attacks, including operations for that purpose;
4. Joint combat development concerning strategic capabilities;
5. Other matters relating to operations to deter and respond to nuclear and weapons-of-mass-destruction attacks.
